(A map holds values under text keys and keeps them in the order they were
 added. A missing key does not crash the program; it raises the error that
 "on error" catches. A map passed as a value keeps its type through the
 call, so it still prints as a map.)

To 'print the record' with a value called record.
    Print record.

A map called person is {"name": "Ada", "age": 36, "city": "London"}.

Print "record:".
Print person.

Print "name is:".
Print person's "name".

Set person's "age" to 37.
Print "after birthday:".
Print person's "age".
Print person's length.

Print "keys:".
For each key in person's keys,
    print key.

Print "values:".
For each detail in person's values,
    print detail.

A map called nested is {"tags": ["a", "b"], "meta": {"id": 1}}.
Print "nested:".
Print nested.
A list called tags is nested's "tags".
Print "tags:".
Print tags.
A map called meta is nested's "meta".
Print "meta id:".
Print meta's "id".

Print "round-trip through a value param:".
'print the record' of person.

Print person's "nope".
On error print "looked up a missing key".
